You are building Step 2 of the Clientloop Phase 1 UI shell plan. Full plan at `/Users/yashbaldha/.claude/plans/zany-mixing-flame.md` — READ IT FIRST for product context, ICP, pricing, and the dossier.

Project: `~/Clientloop` (already scaffolded: Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind v4, shadcn/ui base-nova style). Read `~/Clientloop/CLAUDE.md` for current state.

## Your scope — Step 2 ONLY

Build strict TypeScript types and mock data. No UI. No components. No pages. Just `lib/types.ts` and `lib/mock/*.ts`.

### 1. Create `lib/types.ts`

Strict types — NO `any`, NO optional props unless genuinely optional. Use `as const` where appropriate for literal arrays. Export everything.

Required types (flesh out fields sensibly — these are the minimum):

```ts
export type RequestStatus = "backlog" | "in_progress" | "review" | "delivered";
export type Priority = "low" | "normal" | "high" | "urgent";
export type Plan = "free" | "starter" | "growth" | "scale";
export type ActivityType = "request_created" | "request_delivered" | "client_added" | "request_assigned" | "comment_added" | "brief_generated";
export type TrendDirection = "up" | "down" | "flat";

export interface Client {
  id: string;
  name: string;             // contact person
  email: string;
  avatarUrl: string;        // use https://i.pravatar.cc/128?u=<id> pattern or dicebear
  company: string;
  plan: Plan;
  activeRequests: number;
  mrr: number;              // dollars
  joinedAt: string;         // ISO
}

export interface Service {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  description: string;
  flatPrice: number;        // monthly USD
  turnaroundDays: number;
  category: "design" | "development" | "seo" | "content" | "video" | "ads";
  activeClients: number;
}

export interface Assignee {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  avatarUrl: string;
  role: "owner" | "designer" | "developer" | "pm";
}

export interface Request {
  id: string;
  clientId: string;
  title: string;
  rawMessage: string;       // the unstructured client ask
  status: RequestStatus;
  priority: Priority;
  assigneeId: string;
  createdAt: string;        // ISO
  slaDueAt: string;         // ISO
  tags: readonly string[];
}

export interface KpiMetric {
  id: string;
  label: string;
  value: string;            // already-formatted display value, e.g. "$12,450" or "42"
  rawValue: number;         // numeric for sorting/later charts
  delta: number;            // percent, e.g. 12.4 or -3.1
  trend: TrendDirection;
  iconName: "users" | "inbox" | "activity" | "dollar-sign" | "clock"; // lucide icon name keys
}

export interface ActivityEvent {
  id: string;
  actorId: string;          // references Assignee.id or Client.id
  actorName: string;        // denormalized for rendering
  action: string;           // "delivered", "submitted", "added", etc.
  target: string;           // human-readable target ("Homepage redesign request")
  timestamp: string;        // ISO
  type: ActivityType;
}
```

Feel free to extend with small helper types (e.g. `SlaStatus`) if the dashboard page will need them — but keep it minimal.

### 2. Populate `lib/mock/`

Create these files. All data is **static export consts**, no functions needed except simple getters if useful.

- `lib/mock/assignees.ts` — 4 team members of "Acme Studio" (the demo workspace). Mix of roles.
- `lib/mock/clients.ts` — 12 clients. Mix of Webflow/Framer/SEO agencies from dossier ICP (India/SEA/LATAM skew, some US). Use realistic names, company names, mix of plans (2 free, 4 starter, 4 growth, 2 scale), MRR matching plan tier. JoinedAt dates spread over last 14 months.
- `lib/mock/services.ts` — exactly 6 services:
  1. "Webflow Landing Page" — design — $299 flat — 3 days
  2. "Brand Identity Refresh" — design — $899 flat — 7 days
  3. "SEO Blog Post" — content — $149 flat — 2 days
  4. "Product Explainer Video" — video — $1,499 flat — 10 days
  5. "Full-Stack Feature Dev" — development — $2,499 flat — 14 days
  6. "Google Ads Campaign Setup" — ads — $599 flat — 5 days
  Active client counts should sum to something plausible.
- `lib/mock/requests.ts` — exactly 20 requests distributed: 5 backlog, 7 in_progress, 4 review, 4 delivered. Each has:
  - realistic title matching a service type
  - rawMessage: 1–3 sentences of messy client speak ("hey can u make the hero section pop more and also add testimonials below it thx")
  - priority mix (1 urgent, 4 high, 12 normal, 3 low)
  - assigneeId references real assignees
  - clientId references real clients
  - createdAt within last 21 days
  - slaDueAt: some in the past (breached), some within 24h (warning), most future
  - 1–3 tags each (e.g. "webflow", "rush", "r2-feedback", "v2", "india-ops")
- `lib/mock/metrics.ts` — exactly 5 KPIs matching dashboard plan:
  1. Active Clients: 34, +8.2% up, users icon
  2. Open Requests: 16, -3.1% down, inbox icon
  3. Weekly Active Requests: 22 (the north star from Phase 19), +14.7% up, activity icon
  4. MRR: "$12,450", +11.3% up, dollar-sign icon
  5. Avg SLA: "18.4h", -5.6% down (down is good here), clock icon
- `lib/mock/activity.ts` — 15 events, chronological, last 72 hours, mix of all ActivityType values. Reference real actor names/ids from clients or assignees.

### 3. Helper: `lib/mock/index.ts`

Re-export everything for ergonomic imports: `import { clients, requests, services, assignees, kpiMetrics, activity } from "@/lib/mock"`.

### 4. Verification (MUST run before reporting done)

```
cd ~/Clientloop
pnpm tsc --noEmit
pnpm lint
```

Both must pass with zero errors and zero warnings. If lint complains about unused vars in types.ts or similar, fix it — do not suppress.

### 5. Commit

```
cd ~/Clientloop && git add -A && git commit -m "feat(mock): strict types and seed data for clients, requests, services, metrics, activity"
```

## Hard rules
- NO `any`
- NO `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error`
- NO type assertions (`as X`) except for `as const`
- NO optional fields unless the field is genuinely optional in the domain
- Mock data must be deterministic (hardcoded strings/numbers), NOT generated via `Math.random()` or `faker` — this is static seed data
- IDs should be short stable strings: `c01`, `c02` for clients; `s01` for services; `r01` for requests; `a01` for assignees; `e01` for events; `k01` for KPIs
- Dates: hardcode ISO strings relative to a fixed "now" anchor of `2026-04-10T12:00:00Z` (today per the session). Do NOT use `new Date()`.
- Do not install any new dependencies
- Keep files under 300 lines each — if requests.ts grows too big, that's fine but no bigger

## Report back (under 250 words)
- Files created with line counts
- Paste the output of `pnpm tsc --noEmit` and `pnpm lint` 
- Confirm the git commit hash
- Any deviations and why

